Hi! PhD student here, ecology. I've been fighting with this model for two weeks and I finally have a fit I'm happy with, I think. Background so you know what you're looking at: it's a hierarchical model of seedling survival across 18 forest plots, with plot-level random intercepts, a slope for canopy openness, and a non-centred parameterisation because the centred one had divergences. 4 chains, 2,000 warmup + 2,000 sampling iterations each, adapt_delta = 0.95, zero divergent transitions this time.

```stan
data {
  int<lower=1> N; int<lower=1> J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> plot;
  vector[N] canopy; array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> alive;
}
parameters {
  real alpha; real beta; real<lower=0> sigma_plot;
  vector[J] z_plot;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] a_plot = alpha + sigma_plot * z_plot;
}
model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 1.5); beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_plot ~ exponential(1); z_plot ~ std_normal();
  alive ~ bernoulli_logit(a_plot[plot] + beta * canopy);
}
```

